      "writtenOn": "2016-12-28T22:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hidl-gen does generate these methods on IFoo, IFoo.Proxy and IFoo.Stub as well. But the implementation we care about, the one in the proxy, does need to call through into the actual native transport object, since that is where the magic happens. IFoo.Proxy doesn\u0027t implement a HwRemoteBinder proxy object directly (no multiple inheritance in Java). Instead, it holds a reference to an IHwBinder object in member variable mRemote. So IHwBinder needs these methods, as does HwRemoteBinder (the proxy) - which links them to native method calls.\n\nThis class, the stub base class, does not necessarily need them, since all auto-generated Stub classes already implement (un)linkToDeath. So I\u0027ve removed them here from the new PS.\n\nI do wonder if IFoo.Proxy couldn\u0027t hold a reference to a HwRemoteBinder - since that\u0027s what it is - and in that case we wouldn\u0027t even need these on IHwBinder.",
      "parentUuid": "f7a50a83_0bb028d9",
      "revId": "f200d6900bb8e9ec0bf6749ee52565f0a6139489",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
